      "user": {
        "handle": "Andrew McDiarmid",
        "img_url": "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/93dccb8541d5c8887f8cb2d3e807c2f3?size=240&default=https%3A%2F%2Fs3-alpha.figma.com%2Fstatic%2Fuser_a_v2.png",
        "id": "1217188107541827381"
      },
      "created_at": "2024-09-10T16:45:42.170Z",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "Thanks for looping me in @Ashley Roybal-Reid. From a user trust perspective, I agree that these are the key risks. I expect there is a vocal cohort of \"copy purists\" among Fx users who may bristle at extra content being included when they grab a link to share. That said, there are of course fans that will be happy to evangelize.\n\nConsistent with Mozilla's emphasis on user choice and control, I'd recommend including an opt-out in Fx settings (e.g. \"Include 'sent from Firefox' attribution when sharing links\"), which we could then track to measure the level of frustration.\n\ncc @Emily Wachowiak",
      "reactions": [],
      "client_meta": {
        "node_id": "7109:188",
        "node_offset": {
